<decompilertest>
<!--
    Kuna #1535: AArch64 FCVTMS/FCVTPS were lifted as truncation, so
    (int)floorf(x) and (int)ceilf(x) both printed (int)x and table_lerp's
    lo != hi branch was folded away.  Every scalar, SIMD-scalar and vector
    FCVT{A,M,N,P,Z}{S,U} lifted as TRUNC(x), and FRINT{A,I,M,N,P,X,Z} and
    FRINT32/64{X,Z} stored TRUNC's integer bits in the float register;
    FRINT32/64{X,Z} also left the bits of the vector register above the
    result unchanged.

    First chunk: the issue's exact clang -O2 bytes (floor_i, ceil_i,
    table_lerp).  Second chunk: hand-assembled functions, one per rounding
    mode and width (clang -target aarch64-linux-gnu
    -march=armv8.2-a+fp16):
      round_i   fcvtas w0,s0       rne_i     fcvtns w0,s0
      floor_l   fcvtms x0,d0       ceil_simd fcvtps s0,s0; fmov w0,s0
      floor_f   frintm s0,s0       ceil_d    frintp d0,d0
      round_d   frinta d0,d0       rne_f     frintn s0,s0
      rint_d    frintx d0,d0       nearby_d  frinti d0,d0
      trunc_d   frintz d0,d0       has_frac  frintm/frintp/fcmp/cset ne
      ufloor    fcvtmu w0,s0       vfloor    ldr q0; fcvtms v0.4s; str q0
      uceil_l   fcvtpu x0,d0       floor_h   fcvtms w0,h0
    Third chunk (-march=armv8.5-a):
      f32z_hi   movi v2.2d,#-1; dup v1.2s,v0.s[0]; frint32z v2.2s,v1.2s;
                mov x0,v2.d[1]
      f64x_s    frint64x s1,s0; fmov x0,d1

    Strict SLEIGH fix, no option: M/P/A round with FLOAT_FLOOR/FLOAT_CEIL/
    FLOAT_ROUND (ties away), FCVTZ* truncates, and the float-to-float modes
    p-code has no operator for are the user ops FLOAT_ROUNDEVEN (N),
    FLOAT_TRUNC (FRINTZ), FLOAT_RINT (X) and FLOAT_NEARBYINT (I), typed
    float in and out.  FRINT32/64{X,Z} convert through a 32/64-bit integer
    and zero the register bits above the result.
-->
